 "summary": "Including governor races matters, but how they are tiered does not: the current tiered scheme ranks the 19 runoff pollsters almost the same as presidential + big-8 governors at equal weight (Spearman 0.88), while presidential-only ranks them quite differently (Spearman 0.40 and 0.47). The movers are pollsters whose presidential and governor records diverge (Gerp 14 places, Ipespe 13 places, Veritá 11 places); Futura is first under every scheme. Because shrinkage keeps plus-minus small, the polling-average weight moves by at most 0.29 (Gerp), so the choice changes rankings and grades more than it changes the average."
